[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3658995113","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114064#issuecomment-3658995113","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114064","id":3658995113,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aF9Wp","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-16T06:10:53Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T06:14:13Z","body":"* A duplicate of #74990.\n\nYes, **standard** `Callable`s don't increment the object's reference count. They're simply an `(ObjectID, StringName)` pair representing a method on the instance. As far as I know, this is a deliberate design choice, as otherwise you'd be more likely to encounter memory leaks. For example, you'd have to disconnect all signal connections whose target is the `RefCounted` instance's method so it can be deleted. Signal connections disrupt the hierarchical ownership relationships between objects.\n\nHowever, some **custom** `Callable`s (like GDScript lambdas) increment the reference count. You can wrap a callable method in a lambda if you want a reference instance to prevent it from being deleted.\n\n```gdscript\n## Wraps a method of [RefCounted]-derived object with a lambda.\nstatic func reference_callable(callable: Callable) -> Callable:\n    assert(callable.is_standard())\n    var object: Object = callable.get_object()\n    assert(object is RefCounted)\n    var method: StringName = callable.get_method()\n    return func (...args: Array) -> Variant:\n        return object.callv(method, args)\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3658995113/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3660241935","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114064#issuecomment-3660241935","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114064","id":3660241935,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aKtwP","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-16T12:19:35Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T12:19:35Z","body":"I'm not sure why that is not explained in the documentation with hacks like you provided. GDScript lambdas are broken and leak memory https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102327","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3660241935/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]